## Workflow

1. **Docs first.** Before implementing any new feature, write a plan with the
   key decisions to `docs/implementation/{topic}.md` (see
   `docs/implementation/README.md` for the skeleton) and iterate on it until
   approved. Only then implement.
2. **Docs stay true.** Every change that affects behavior updates the relevant
   `docs/implementation/*.md` and the routing table below **in the same
   change**. Out-of-date docs are treated as bugs.
3. **Test what is exact.** Business logic, data transformations, and utilities
   get unit tests — written with or before the implementation. Do not write UI
   snapshot/visual tests; UI is verified by hand or E2E where it exists.
4. **Self-documenting code.** One-sentence description above every non-trivial
   function/component. Non-obvious hacks are documented inline with a
   reference to what forces them.
5. When a mistake gets corrected in review, propose a rule for this file so it
   is never repeated.

## Routing table

When looking for something, start here — and extend this table whenever a new
significant location appears:

| Looking for… | Location |
| --- | --- |
| Feature plans & decisions | `docs/implementation/` |
| Pages & URL routes | `src/app/` (App Router — folder = route) |
| Root layout & provider tree | `src/app/layout.tsx`, `src/app/providers.tsx` |
